  "criteriaReviewed": {
    "completeAnatomy": "Whole original model head, jaw, neck, clavicles and shoulders remain visually continuous across variants. No independent neck cut, cap, tapered tab or floating-head appearance found.",
    "ageAnatomy": "Infants retain soft short-neck swaddled models, children retain actual child proportions, and middle/elder skin, neck and arms retain their source ageing.",
    "collarsAndSleeves": "No material collar gap, ghost slit, detached shoulder or disconnected forearm found. Child work outfits read as layered clothing. Navy aristocrat registration and purple/gold royalty fit original neck openings.",
    "skinPalette": "Face, ears, neck and arms read as continuous skin under the painted light. No broad forehead/cheek panel, eye island or hard diagonal forearm recolour boundary found. Gray hair/beards remain natural.",
    "mixedPixelFinish": "Fine2px facial region retains eye/pupil structure at native output size; coarse3px body remains stylistically consistent with no material visible patch edge.",
    "wardrobeReadability": "Ten adult groups are distinguishable, including retained gold elite, navy aristocrat and purple/gold royalty."
  },
